Statements:
[
    "The goals are non-blocking logging, durable and queryable storage, the ability to attach late signals to past conversations, and PII masking before storage.",
    "A recommended log schema uses a row-per-turn format with core fields.",
    "The core fields include conversation_id, session_id, user_id, turn_id, timestamp, role, text_masked, pii_masked, pii_types_masked, metadata, computed_signals, captured_signals, and storage_id.",
    "conversation_id is a unique id for the whole conversation or session.",
    "session_id is the session instance id if it is different from the conversation.",
    "user_id is a user identifier, pseudonymous if required.",
    "turn_id is the turn number within a conversation.",
    "timestamp records when the turn occurred in ISO8601 format.",
    "role is an enum with values user, assistant, or system.",
    "text_masked is the utterance text with PII removed or masked.",
    "pii_masked indicates whether masking was applied.",
    "pii_types_masked lists the PII types masked, such as phone, card, or aadhaar.",
    "metadata stores routing, model_version, latencies, and flags.",
    "computed_signals stores values such as sentiment, intent_confidence, and heuristics.",
    "captured_signals stores event captures like button_clicks and rating.",
    "storage_id is the primary key or internal log id.",
    "A separate late-signal table should store one row per signal.",
    "The late-signal table includes late_signal_id, conversation_id, attach_to_turn_id, signal_type, signal_timestamp, signal_payload, source, and processed_flag.",
    "late_signal_id identifies the late signal.",
    "conversation_id links the late signal to the conversation_id in the main table.",
    "attach_to_turn_id optionally identifies which turn the signal refers to.",
    "signal_type can be escalation_email, support_ticket, or refund.",
    "signal_timestamp records when the late signal happened in ISO8601 format.",
    "signal_payload contains masked details about the signal.",
    "source identifies where the signal came from, such as email or support_system.",
    "processed_flag indicates whether the signal has been attached and reconciled.",
    "To make logging non-blocking, PII should be masked immediately at the edge before leaving the request path.",
    "Log events should be pushed asynchronously to an in-memory buffer, event stream, or background worker.",
    "The response path should not synchronously wait for the durable write.",
    "A background writer should write batched events into the durable, queryable store.",
